cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this prototype or its design, please cite it as below."
title: "Layout-Aware-Retrieval: Page-Native Layout Regions as a Verifiable Retrieval Unit for Engineering Datasheets"
abstract: >-
  A retrieval pipeline for layout-bearing technical documents. The unit of
  retrieval is a page-native layout region — a group of detected layout elements
  read as one unit — rather than a fixed-length token window. Document identity,
  page number, PDF-point bounding boxes, native text, section path, and a rendered
  evidence image travel together as a single inspectable evidence package, so every
  result can be checked against the exact region of the exact page it came from.
  Retrieval fuses a multilingual dense index with a part-number-aware BM25 index by
  Reciprocal Rank Fusion. No quantitative evaluation has been run; the protocol that
  would produce one is pre-registered in the repository and contains no results.
